ray as="points"><mxPoint x="1610" y="595"/><mxPoint x="1610" y="400"/></Array><mxPoint x="1600" y="595" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1590" y="400" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="11-86" value="wclr" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontSize=10;" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="11-85"><mxGeometry x="0.3" y="0" relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint as="offset"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="11-87" value="full[1:0] goes back to every writer: a core starts a group only when full[bank] = 0 (S_WAIT, F_WAIT, E_WAIT). With two streams core 0 fills bank 0 (even groups) and core 1 bank 1 (odd groups); with one stream core 0 alternates the banks; MATMUL uses only the tensor core." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="660" y="560" width="620" height="70" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="11-88" value="Early release: the MAC clears full[b] (wclr) when it starts the last row of the group. The next writer of bank b starts at least 2 cycles later and writes at most 1 word per 4 cycles, while the MAC reads 1 word per cycle without stalling → it always stays behind the read pointer (t_wd checks every read and counts these overlaps)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="660" y="640" width="960" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="11-89" value="u85m_wd_raw8 (rtl/wd/u85m_wd_raw8.sv) — state_e {S_IDLE, S_WAIT, S_RUN}" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=2;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#666666;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="430" width="600" height="280" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="11-90" value="S_IDLE" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=